^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
When the inner dimension of a two-dimensional array is variable-length, the
array is handled by the array theory, and a read at indices that equal the
indices of a preceding write, but are different terms, is not constrained to
yield the written value: the propositional back-end reports a spurious
counterexample. With --z3, the assertion is proved.
